node_modules/
# ⚠️ ANCHORED. A bare `dist/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently
# swallowed `dist-plugin/dist/` — the compiled CLI that ships inside the plugin. The plugin
# would have installed with no CLI at all, and nothing would have said so.
/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build / test output
*.tgz
coverage/
*.log

# Local environment
.env
.env.*

# ⚠️ `dist-plugin/` is BUILD OUTPUT that is COMMITTED on purpose. Claude Code installs a plugin
# by fetching this repository; there is no build step on the way in, so anything not committed
# does not exist for the user. `npm run build:plugin` regenerates it, and `plugin-build.test.js`
# fails if what is committed differs from what the templates produce.
# ⚠️ `CLAUDE.md` is COMMITTED. It is rendered from `.ds/` by `ds sync --write`, and `ds check`
# verifies it against the model — so a clone without it reports a missing artifact, and a teammate
# gets no pointer at the index. Never edit it by hand; regenerate it.
.ds/config.json
CLAUDE.local.md
